1. gpui-ce (Butler fork)
------------------------
Source: https://github.com/Hexpy-Games/gpui-ce, branch feat/butler-port-gaps
(rev d4e3761e6860de9feb35dde6df944635ff90a4f2), a fork of
https://github.com/gpui-ce/gpui-ce, which derives from GPUI by Zed Industries.
License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0;
the text is LICENSE.md in that repository). Its NOTICE file reads:

    gpui-ce, Butler fork
    Copyright 2026 HexpyGames (헥스피게임즈)

    This repository is a fork of gpui-ce (https://github.com/gpui-ce/gpui-ce),
    which derives from GPUI by Zed Industries. gpui-ce and this fork are
    licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE.md and the
    LICENSE-APACHE files of the crates). The fork's base is gpui-ce commit
    94791b8882f88c126b3089759cb7829a9c1de1a2; its changes are on the
    butler/lens branch, under the same license.

    Changes made by HexpyGames (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)). Every
    changed file starts with a notice line.

    - Backdrop lens: liquid-glass refraction through a continuous distance
      field, dispersion, frost, rim light, tone curve, full-shape detail
      pass and hairline ring, with per-lens backdrop snapshots (gpui scene,
      plan and window; gpui_render blur, build and shaders; gpui_wgpu
      renderer; gpui_windows DirectX renderer).
    - Procedural wallpaper passes, run only when a wallpaper's generation
      changes (gpui scene and window; gpui_render shaders; gpui_wgpu and
      gpui_windows wallpapers.rs, added).
    - Drop shadows clipped to outside their element (gpui scene and window;
      gpui_render shadows shader).
    - DirectWrite: grayscale and colour glyphs rasterized unhinted with
      symmetric anti-aliasing (gpui_windows direct_write.rs).
    - Windows window: the Acrylic backdrop, the minimized state, the
      display refresh rate and the app's light/dark override (gpui
      platform.rs and window.rs; gpui_windows window, platform, events,
      util and display).
    - Native window buttons: whether the platform draws the window's own
      minimize, zoom and close buttons (gpui platform.rs and window.rs;
      gpui_macos window.rs), and Acrylic drawn as the macOS sidebar
      vibrancy (gpui_macos window.rs).
    - IME focus changes: gpui reports a move between text inputs
      (TextInputStateChange::FocusMoved); macOS discards and Windows
      completes the input method's composition on focus change without
      delivering it; the Windows candidate window excludes the caret line
      and answers IMR_QUERYCHARPOSITION (gpui platform.rs, window.rs and
      input.rs; gpui_web window.rs; gpui_macos window.rs; gpui_windows
      window.rs and events.rs).
    - Headless tests: a configurable window scale factor (gpui test
      platform and window, HeadlessAppContext).
    - EditableText accessibility and IME: inputs forward their ARIA
      properties, expose one text run per visual line with character
      positions and widths, answer IME rectangle queries from the previous
      layout until the next layout, and end their composition when they
      lose focus (gpui div.rs; gpui_elements editable_text element and
      state).
    - EditableText native field behaviour: presses are hit-tested, the
      caret stays in view after edits, multiline input stores LF line
      breaks, the IME composition uses the font's 1-px underline, and the
      selection paints under the text and fills continued lines to the
      field edge, and hosts can clear the undo history (gpui_elements
      editable_text element, state, layout and history).
    - EditableText caret: edits reveal the caret's whole line, and the
      caret is hidden while text is selected (gpui_elements editable_text
      element and state).
    - EditableText layout: measuring at several widths in one frame keeps
      the layout of the final width (gpui_elements editable_text element).

    The lens model was written with reference to these MIT-licensed
    projects; no code was copied from them:
    - LiquidGlass by ybouane, https://github.com/ybouane/liquidglass
    - liquidGL by NaughtyDuk, https://github.com/naughtyduk/liquidGL
    - Liquid Glass Studio by iyinchao,
      https://github.com/iyinchao/liquid-glass-studio

    Third-party notices that came with gpui-ce remain in place, for example
    crates/gpui_render/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

